files that said MIT; see Part E).

Note: this license is written in plain English. It is not legal advice, and the
owner of JavCMS may have it checked by a lawyer.

In short: use it for free, also for your own website that earns money. Copy it,
change it and share it. Do not sell it, and do not charge other people for
installing, setting up, running, supporting, changing or handing over JavCMS.
Copies that you share stay free and carry no money-making code or links of
yours.


PART A. THE JAVCMS COMMUNITY LICENSE 1.0
----------------------------------------

1. What this license covers

   "JavCMS" in this license means the work of the JavCMS project in this package:
   - the code that JavCMS wrote;
   - the changes that JavCMS made to MacCMS files (the changes only, not the
     original MacCMS code);
   - the JavCMS work on the themes in the template/ folder (see Part D);
   - the JavCMS documentation (README, INSTALL, UPGRADE, CHANGELOG, docs/).

   It does not cover third-party components. They keep their own licenses
   (see Parts B and C). Changes that JavCMS made inside a third-party file
   whose license requires changed versions to stay under that license (for
   example the LGPL of the editor libraries, PclZip and PHP QR Code) are
   under that license, not under this one. Changes that JavCMS made inside
   other third-party files (for example ThinkPHP, CodeMirror, UMeditor and
   Layui files; NOTICE.CHANGED-FILES.txt lists them) are covered by this
   license in the same way as its changes to MacCMS files: the changes only,
   while the original code in those files keeps its own license.

2. What you may do

   Anyone may, free of charge:
   - use JavCMS, also for your own websites that earn money, for example with
     ads (a website of your own company, or of an organisation that employs
     you or that you volunteer for without pay, counts as your own website; a
     customer's or client's website does not, even when you are paid to work
     on it: a contractor, freelancer or business that is paid to install, set
     up, run or change JavCMS for someone else is not using it for its own
     website);
   - copy JavCMS;
   - change JavCMS;
   - share JavCMS, changed or unchanged, under the conditions in section 4.

3. What nobody may do: sell JavCMS

   Nobody may ask for or take money, or any other payment, for:
   - copies or downloads of JavCMS;
   - changed versions of JavCMS;
   - JavCMS themes, or any part of JavCMS;
   - installation packages that contain JavCMS;
   - access to copies of JavCMS (the software itself) behind a paywall (for
     example a paid download area or a paid membership that is needed to get
     JavCMS), or access to them that is only given in exchange for something
     else of value (for example watching ads, filling in paid surveys or
     passing through paid link shorteners);
   - installing, setting up or handing over JavCMS, or a changed version of it,
     for other people (for example a paid installation or setup service, or a
     website with JavCMS that is built for a customer and handed over);
   - support for JavCMS, or running, customizing or changing JavCMS or its
     themes, for other people (for example paid support, paid management of
     someone else's JavCMS website, paid customization or paid changes; what
     counts as your own website is said in section 2);
   - hosting plans or other services that come with JavCMS installed or set
     up (a host whose customers install JavCMS themselves is fine).

   Charging for any of these counts as selling JavCMS. So does earning money
   with copies of JavCMS that you share, through money-making code or links
   built into them (section 4). Free help is available from the JavCMS
   community: https://t.me/avdb_api

   Allowed: running your own website with JavCMS and earning money with that
   website, for example with ads or with paid areas of that website (section 2).
   The rules above are about JavCMS itself, not about the content of your
   website. You may also sell a website that you have really run yourself (its
   domain, content and audience), as long as JavCMS on it stays free under
   this license with every notice kept and no price is asked for JavCMS
   itself. Building or setting up JavCMS websites in order to sell them is not
   allowed.

4. Conditions when you share JavCMS

   When you share JavCMS or a changed version of it:
   - it must stay free of charge (section 3);
   - it must not carry money-making code or links of the person who shares it
     (or of anyone that person works with): no ads, affiliate or referral
     codes, paid or sold links (backlinks), cryptocurrency miners, or tracking
     whose data is sold to others, built into the copy. This is not about the
     notices and links that come with JavCMS itself (keep the notices), and
     running your own website with JavCMS, with your own ads on that website,
     stays allowed (section 2);
   - it must stay under this same license, and you must include this LICENSE
     file and the NOTICE file;
   - you must keep every copyright, license and source notice, including the
     short notice at the top of the JavCMS files;
   - you must mark your changes: say in the changed files, or in a list that
     comes with your copy, which files you changed.

5. No warranty

   JavCMS is provided "as is", without any warranty. The authors are not liable
   for any damage or loss that comes from using it.

6. End of your rights

   If you break this license, your rights under it end automatically. People
   who received JavCMS from that person keep their rights, as long as they
   follow this license.

7. Files that said "MIT" in earlier releases, and files with third-party code

   Some JavCMS files said "MIT" in their header in earlier releases: the
   visitor theme switcher, the auto-icon system, the FX kit, the stylesheets
   and scripts of the seven *-modern themes, and some JavCMS artwork and
   animations. From release 1.2.0 these files are under this license as
   well, and their headers and folder license files say so. Copies of them
   from releases up to and including 1.1.0 stay under the MIT license (see
   Part E).

   A JavCMS file that contains third-party code says so in its short notice
   ("Contains third-party code under its own license, named in NOTICE", or
   "Partly based on a third-party theme" for theme files). For such a file,
   this license covers only the JavCMS parts; the third-party code keeps its
   own license, and NOTICE or Part D names it. A MacCMS file that
   contains a measurable share of changes from the MacCMS editions RamCMS
   and/or ApiiCMS says so in its notice ("with changes from the MacCMS
   editions RamCMS (Apache-2.0) and/or ApiiCMS (MIT)"); smaller traces may be
   in other changed MacCMS files, which carry the usual MacCMS notice. Those
   changes keep their own licenses (Parts B and C).

8. Contributions

   If you send changes to the JavCMS project, you agree that they may be used
   and shared under this license.


PART B. PARTS THAT STAY UNDER THE APACHE LICENSE 2.0
---------------------------------------------------

The following parts are not JavCMS work. They keep the Apache License 2.0. The
no-sale rule in Part A does not apply to them: under the Apache License 2.0,
anyone may use, change, share and also sell these parts on their own, as long as
they follow that license.

- MacCMS 10 by magicblack (https://github.com/magicblack/maccms10): the original
  MacCMS code that JavCMS is based on (base release v2023.1000.3051).
  Copyright 2014-2021 magicblack. The original MacCMS notice is kept below,
  word for word. A few image files come from later MacCMS releases under the
  same license: static/images/pro/lang-en.png, lang-zh.png and paly.png
  (v2026.1000.4056) and static/images/signin_ic_account.png,
  signin_ic_code.png and signin_ic_password.png (v2024.1000.4046).
- ThinkPHP 5.0.24 (thinkphp/): Copyright 2006-2018 ThinkPHP (thinkphp.cn),
  liu21st.
- topthink think-captcha, think-helper, think-image, think-installer and
  think-queue, and karsonzhang fastadmin-addons (vendor/). The six captcha
  fonts that the MacCMS release ships with think-captcha are freeware fonts of
  other authors (one of them is free for personal use only); they are not part
  of think-captcha's license and are not in this package. Its captcha font
  folder (vendor/topthink/think-captcha/assets/ttfs/) holds a copy of the
  Droid Sans Mono font named below instead, and the unused captcha background
  photos (assets/bgs/), whose origin is not known, are left out.
- hls.js 1.7.3 and 0.9.1, flv.js 1.4.2 and Video.js 7.4.1 (with vtt.js), used by
  the players and the ad engine.
- Remix Icon 4.8.0 glyphs inside the JavCMS icon sprites
  (static/template-ui/auto-icon/) and in the sprites of crimson-modern and
  onyx-modern (template/crimson-modern/assets/icons.svg,
  template/onyx-modern/assets/icons.svg).
- Material Icons path data (Google, https://github.com/google/material-design-icons)
  in the topaz icon sprite template/topaz/assets/img/icons.svg.
- The Droid Sans Mono font static/font/test.ttf (Digitized data copyright ©
  2007, Google Corporation), the default font of the text watermark, shipped
  by MacCMS. From release 1.2.0 a copy of it is also the captcha font
  (vendor/topthink/think-captcha/assets/ttfs/DroidSansMono.ttf).
- Not in this package: the Flash video player static/player/play.swf of the
  MacCMS release (Vcastr 3.0, Apache License 2.0 on its project page, with
  TweenLite / TweenFilterLite and a pixel font inside whose licenses the file
  does not state) and its player stub static/player/flv.js; current browsers no
  longer run Flash.
- RamCMS (https://github.com/cinohub/ramcms, formerly
  https://github.com/brevisnguyen/ramcms), a Vietnamese edition of MacCMS 10
  by Brevis Nguyen. Its license file is the MacCMS notice below (Apache License
  2.0); it adds no copyright line of its own. Some changes that RamCMS made to
  MacCMS files are in JavCMS, mostly through ApiiCMS (Part C); the files with a
  measurable share say so in their notice.
- The OAuth login classes in extend/login/ (MacCMS classes that JavCMS
  rewrote) stay under the Apache License 2.0, as their headers say.

JavCMS changed some of these files. NOTICE and NOTICE.CHANGED-FILES.txt list
those changes.

Original MacCMS notice (kept as section 4 of the Apache License 2.0 requires):

