images), the DashLite admin stylesheet, the fancyBox 2.1.5 stylesheet and
images, the Pear Admin Layui files, layui_dropdown, jquery.lang.js, and the
theme JAVCMS Classic (Part D). NOTICE.CHANGED-FILES.txt lists the files of the
MacCMS release and of the bundled libraries among them.


PART D. WHERE THE THEMES COME FROM
----------------------------------

- jav, jav-modern and javcms-modern are older JavCMS themes, built on
  third-party themes:
  - javcms-modern ("JAVCMS Modern", the default theme of this package) keeps
    the page markup of a third-party tube theme made for KVS (Kernel Video
    Sharing) that had been adapted to MacCMS; who made that theme and the
    adaptation, and under which license, is not known. The javcms-modern page
    templates whose notice says "partly based on a third-party theme" keep
    that markup (header, menu, video and article lists); JavCMS claims no
    rights in it. Its stylesheets (gallery.css, jc-core.css, jc-skin.css,
    surface.css) and scripts were written by JavCMS.
  - JAVCMS Classic (template/javcms), the default theme up to release 1.1.0,
    is not in this package from release 1.2.0. It was built on the same tube
    theme and loaded that theme's base stylesheet (ksassets/css/main.css; some
    of its rules are the same as rules of the KVS default theme of the Kernel
    Team), its IcoMoon icon font (ksassets/font/icomoon.*) and orang.css, a
    stylesheet of the 8X default_pc theme pack with that pack's icon font;
    their authors and licenses are not known. Sites that upgrade keep their
    own copy of it (UPGRADE.md). Earlier releases also carried the fancyBox
    2.1.5 stylesheet and its four images in that theme (non-commercial use
    only).
  - The page templates of jav and jav-modern were built on stui-based
    third-party MacCMS templates (heisejianyue and xigua111, as shipped by
    RamCMS); JavCMS claims no rights in that work. The stylesheets of jav and
    jav-modern were written by JavCMS; they style the class names of that
    framework. Up to release 1.1.0 jav also carried the play button image
    statics/img/play.png of the heisejianyue template and a background strip
    of unknown origin for its watch page (statics/img/play_bg.webp); from
    release 1.2.0 both are images made by JavCMS.
  - Some user pages of these three themes share layout with stock X4 / 8X
    theme pages.
- ember, onyx, velvet, honey, neon, crimson and topaz were rebuilt by JavCMS
  from third-party MacCMS theme packs: 8X / X4 / default_pc (ember), MDblack
  (onyx), MDkm (velvet), MDYouTiao (honey), MDXiangJiao (neon), MDLutu
  (crimson) and hanime.zip (topaz). The templates, styles and scripts were
  written again by JavCMS, but the designs come from those packs, and a few
  files keep parts of them: the user pages of ember and honey (see below) and
  the topaz stylesheet assets/css/topaz.css, which reuses a number of rules of
  the hanime stylesheet (html/style/css/application.css). Up to release 1.1.0
  the neon theme also used 42 icon images of the original MDXiangJiao pack
  (template/neon/assets/img/icons/); from release 1.2.0 the 14 that neon shows
  are images made by JavCMS, and the other 28, which nothing used, are left
  out.
- The seven *-modern themes (ember-modern, onyx-modern, velvet-modern,
  honey-modern, neon-modern, crimson-modern, topaz-modern) were designed for
  JavCMS on the same template set.

The JavCMS license covers the JavCMS work on these themes: its code, its
changes and its own designs. It does not cover the work of the original theme
authors, and it gives no rights in that work. Files that still contain the work
of an original theme author say so in their notice ("partly based on a
third-party theme"); this includes the user-centre, payment, confirm and
similar pages of jav, ember and honey (and their -modern twins) and of
javcms-modern that still share layout and script with stock theme pages
(among them the user info, menu, sign-in and password pages of ember, jav and
javcms-modern), the article pages art/detail, art/ajax_detail, art/type,
art/hot, art/indexhot and art/new of jav and jav-modern, which keep the page
skeleton of the xigua111 template, the javcms-modern templates that keep the
markup of the KVS tube theme (header, menu, video and article lists), the
user-centre stylesheets of ember and ember-modern, which restyle the FED
framework of the 8X user pages, and the topaz stylesheet assets/css/topaz.css.
Template files whose shared parts come from MacCMS itself say "Based on MacCMS
10" instead; among them are the RSS and sitemap templates (html/rss/) of every
theme, except five of jav and five of jav-modern: baidu.html, bing.html,
sm.html, so.html and sogou.html there are ApiiCMS templates
(template/mrphim/html/rss/ in ApiiCMS), unchanged apart from spaces, so they
carry no JavCMS notice (see NOTICE); google.html and index.html of these two
themes are JavCMS rewrites of the MacCMS templates.


